WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:03.234
- Samuel L. Jackson, where are you?

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:04.166
(audience cheers)

00:00:04.166 --> 00:00:05.630
(Denzel whoops)

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.373
Samuel L. Jackson.

00:00:08.478 --> 00:00:11.853
(chuckles) Nah, I'm not gonna do that.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.840
Let me tell you something.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:19.190
We go back so far, but
I'll start with this,

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:23.070
152 movie titles,

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:24.469
I got IMDb Pro.

00:00:24.469 --> 00:00:26.590
(audience laughs)

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:29.760
152 movie titles,

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:34.760
27 billion in box office.

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:36.253
27 billion,

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:43.220
more than any other actor in history,

00:00:43.223 --> 00:00:45.160
(audience cheers)

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.453
Samuel L. Jackson.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.903
11 times, Nick Fury.

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:56.453
One time, Django.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:01.000
I just like saying Django
'cause he says Django,

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.483
I just like Django.

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:08.223
Sam and I go back in the theater,

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.780
the Goodman Theater.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:13.530
We worked together even before that

00:01:14.553 --> 00:01:16.240
at the Negro Ensemble Company,

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.240
we did a pretty good play
called "A Soldier's Play,"

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.590
that became a great movie,
"A Soldier's Story."

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.540
Wasn't as good as it would've
been had Sam been in it,

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:30.540
but that's for another day. (laughs)

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.233
That's for another day.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.535
What else I got on here?

00:01:35.535 --> 00:01:37.660
(audience laughs)

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.580
Many awards, obviously.

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:42.500
Big box office, you know all about that.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:43.850
Here's what you don't know.

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:48.080
These are, and there's a few of them,

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:51.610
the organizations that Samuel L. Jackson

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.973
and his wife, LaTanya Jackson, give to:

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:59.080
Alzheimer's Association, American
Institute for Stuttering,

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:01.713
American Red Cross, Artists
for a New South Africa,

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:05.060
Bedford-Stuyvesant
Restoration Corporation,

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.280
Black Economic Alliance,

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.030
The Brain Trust, Cedars-Sinai,

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:10.470
Broadway Cares/Equity Fights AIDS,

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:12.910
Carousel of Hope, Children's Defense Fund,

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:17.540
Desmond and, and somebody
Tutu Legacy Foundation,

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:18.750
Earth Island Foundation,

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:22.210
the HollyRod Foundation for
Autism and Parkinson's Disease,

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:23.690
In a Perfect World Foundation,

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:25.660
The Joseph Lowery Institute
for Social Change,

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:28.390
Magic Johnson Foundation, Spelman College,

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:30.950
Morehouse College, NAACP
Legal Defense Fund,

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.020
National Action Network,

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:34.120
Kidney Foundation, Solutions Coalition,

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.830
the Smithsonian National Museum
of African American History,

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:38.660
Spelman College United Nero College Fund,

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:40.760
and the Urban League.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.593
(audience cheers)

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:49.420
That's what he's been doing,

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:50.677
I don't know what y'all been doing.

00:02:50.677 --> 00:02:52.130
(audience laughs)

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:53.730
But that's what he's been doing.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.890
Make sure I didn't forget anything now.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:02:59.860
Oh, I'm supposed to look up here.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:01.480
Now,

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:05.793
now let's look over just a
few of his greatest moments.

